Spring Core:
@Component → Marks a class as bean
@Service → Business logic layer bean
@Repository → DAO bean, exception translation
@Controller → Web MVC controller
@RestController → Controller + @ResponseBody
@Autowired → Dependency injection
@Qualifier → Choose between multiple beans
@Bean → Create a bean inside config class
@Configuration → Java config file
@Value → Read value from application.properties
@ComponentScan → Scans packages for beans
@Lazy -> Bean gets created only when needed.

Spring Boot Core:
@SpringBootApplication → Combines @Configuration, @EnableAutoConfiguration, @ComponentScan
@EnableAutoConfiguration → Auto config beans based on classpath
@ConfigurationProperties → Map properties to Java class
CommandLineRunner → Run code at startup
ApplicationRunner → Alternative to CommandLineRunner
@Profile → Run beans for specific environments (dev, prod)
@ConditionalOnMissingBean → Create bean only if missing
@ConditionalOnProperty → Create bean based on property

Spring MVC:
@GetMapping → Handle GET request
@PostMapping → Handle POST request
@PutMapping → Handle PUT request
@DeleteMapping → Handle DELETE request
@RequestMapping → Generic mapping
@PathVariable → Read from URL path
@RequestParam → Read query params
@RequestBody → Read JSON body
@ResponseBody → Return JSON
@ModelAttribute → Bind form data
@CrossOrigin → Enable CORS
@ExceptionHandler → Handle specific exceptions
@ControllerAdvice → Global exception handling

Spring Data JPA:
@Entity → Database table
@Table → Custom table name
@Id → Primary key
@GeneratedValue → Auto ID
@Column → Map column
@OneToOne, @OneToMany, @ManyToOne, @ManyToMany → Relationships
@JoinColumn → Foreign key
@Transactional → Open transaction
@EnableJpaRepositories → Enable JPA repos
JpaRepository → CRUD + pagination + sorting

Spring Security
@EnableWebSecurity → Enable security config
@BeanSecurityFilterChain → Core configuration in Spring Security 6+
@PreAuthorize → Method-level authorization
@PostAuthorize → After method execution authorization
@EnableMethodSecurity → Enable method-level security
@AuthenticationPrincipal → Get logged-in user
UserDetailsService → Load user from DB
PasswordEncoder → Hash passwords
@CrossOrigin (CORS) → Allow frontend domains
CORS->Allow frontend domains to call backend.

JWT filters (Custom):
OncePerRequestFilter → For JWT
AuthenticationEntryPoint → Handle unauthorized

TRANSACTIONS (Spring @Transactional)
@Transactional	->Makes method run inside a transaction.
Rollback	->Occurs automatically on RuntimeException.
propagation=REQUIRED->	Join existing transaction or create new.
propagation=REQUIRES_NEW->	Always create new transaction.
Isolation level	->Controls how concurrent DB reads/writes behave.
